## 2.2 Synthesis of MOFs
Synthesis of MOF 1. ${\bf B a C l}_{2}{\cdot}2{\bf H}_{2}{\bf O}$ $\mathrm{(0.1~mmol)}$ , $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{L}1$ 1 $\left(0.05\ \mathrm{mmol}\right)$ , DMF $(6~\mathrm{ml})$ and $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ $3~\mathrm{ml}$ ) were heated at $120~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for 3 days in $15~\mathrm{ml}$ steel reactor and then cooled to the ambient condition $(10\ ^{\circ}\mathbf{C}{\cdot}\mathbf{h}^{-1})$ . The block products were formed (yield $98\%$ ). Elemental analysis (EA) of MOF 1, calculated $(\%)$ : C, 32.74; H, 2.497; N, 6.942. Found: C, 32.31; H, 2.362; N, 6.923. Fourier transform infrared (IR) $(\mathrm{cm}^{-1})$ (Fig. S1): 3591 (m), 3120 (w), 1569 (s), 1379 (w), 1241 (s), 1061 (m), 769 (w), 663 (w).
