thermally stable up to $\sim189^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ and the next weight loss of $7.5\%$ (cal. $8.0\%$ ) because of the loss of DMF molecules. Powder $\mathrm{\Delta}\mathrm{X}$ -ray diffraction (PXRD) patterns of the two MOFs were well consistent with their simulated patterns of the X-ray crystal data (Fig. S6). Under a high vacuum, the sample MOF 2 was heated to $100~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $^\textrm{\scriptsize1h}$ and $175~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $^{2\mathrm{~h~}}$ to get the solvent-exclusion product of MOF 2a, and the PXRD pattern of MOF 2a is the same with original PXRD pattern of MOF 2, confirming that the main framework of MOF 2 is intact after removing the guest molecules. The IR and TGA test also prove that there is absence of DMF solvent of MOF 2a (Figs. S2, S5c).
## 3.3 Gas adsorption behaviors
The gas capture capacities were studied carefully because there are high density of active sites and Lewis acid metal sites in MOF 2. Firstly, the $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ and $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ capture experiments of MOF 2a were tested at 195, 273 and $298\mathrm{~K~}$ . At $195\mathrm{~K~}$ , the $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ sorption value of MOF 2a reaches $146.7~\mathrm{cm}^{3}{\cdot}\mathrm{g}^{-1}$ (Fig. 4a). According to the Horvath–Kawazoe model, the curve of the size distribution of channel is calculated (Fig. S7), and the BET and Langmuir surface areas of MOF 2a are calculated to be 471 and $646~\mathrm{cm}^{2}{\cdot}\mathrm{g}^{-1}$ , respectively. The total pore volume of MOF 2a is $0.268~\mathrm{cm}^{3}{\cdot}\mathbf{g}^{-1}$ calculated by $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ isotherm $(p/p_{0}=0.989)$ ), and the value is comparable with the total pore volume $(0.256~\mathrm{cm}^{3}{\cdot}\mathbf{g}^{-1})$ obtained by crystal structure [16–19].
At 273 and $298\mathrm{~K~}$ under $100\mathrm{Pa}$ , the $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ capture amount of MOF 2a is 101.01 and $55.08~\mathrm{cm}^{3}{\cdot}\mathrm{g}^{-1}$ (Fig. 4b), respectively, which overpass many reported cases that the MOFs with tubular channels have high density of open Lewis acid metallic sites at $273\mathrm{~K~}$ [20, 21]. Especially, there also exist the hysteresis phenomena in MOF 2a, indicating the adsorbed gas species are not released immediately and trapped in the framework at the lower pressure, and the probable reason of which should be attributed to the interactions of the $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ and N-rich groups as well as the $\mathbf{Ba(II)}$ ions [22]. Nevertheless, MOF 2a only exhibits a little capture of $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ (28.03 and $13.65~\mathrm{cm}^{3}{\cdot}\mathrm{g}^{-1}\gamma$ ).
The reason for this phenomenon is because that the kinetic diameter of $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ $(0.33~\mathrm{nm})$ is less than that of $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ $(0.38~\mathrm{nm})$ , which may boost the $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ high uptake. In order to explore the affinity of the skeleton to gas molecules, the isosteric heat $(Q_{\mathrm{st}})$ of $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ capture was obtained via the Clausius–Clapeyron equation (Fig. S8). The $\boldsymbol{Q}_{\mathrm{st}}$ values of $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ are much higher than that of $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ (Fig. 5), showing that the interactions between the main skeleton and $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ molecules are much stronger than those of framework and $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ molecules. The quadrupole moment and higher polarizability of $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ are the reasons for its higher $\boldsymbol{Q}_{\mathrm{st}}$ (quadrupole moment: $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ of $1.43\times10^{-39}\mathrm{{C}}{\cdot}\mathrm{{m}}^{2}.$ , $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ of 0 $\mathbf{C}{\cdot}\mathbf{m}^{2}$ ; polarizability: $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ of $29.1\times10^{-25}\ \mathrm{cm}^{-3}$ , $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ of $25.9\times10^{-25}\mathrm{~cm}^{-3}.$ .) [23].
To imitate the separation behavior of MOF 2a under a more real-world circumstance, the gas selectivity of $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/$ $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ was calculated via IAST model at 273 and $298\mathrm{~K~}$ (Figs. S9, S10) under $100\mathrm{Pa}$ , respectively, and the separation coefficients of $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ are 25 and 13 at 273 and
$298\mathrm{~K~}$ for the equal molar gas mixtures (Fig. 6). In addition, the content of $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ ranges from $20\%$ to $80\%$ with the selectivity of 25–28 at $273\mathrm{~K~}$ (Fig. S11); meanwhile, the selectivity of $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ with the molar ratio of 2:8 and 8:2 is 17 and 3 at $298\mathrm{~K~}$ , respectively (Fig. S12). The high separation of $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ is mainly attributed to the $\mathbf{Ba(II)}$ ions as well as the abundant uncoordinated $\mathbf{N}$ atoms trapped in the porous surface of the channels, making the highly polar host framework and the guest $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ molecules to be interlocked firmly as well as simultaneously to enhance the electrostatic interactions of the porous surface and $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ species [24–30].
## 4 Conclusion
In conclusion, two related comparable new MOFs were yielded by self-assembly of $\mathbf{Ba(II)}$ ions and two similar ligands, respectively. Herein, MOF 1 presents a 3D stacking motif, while MOF 2 has a 3D nanotube porous motif with the cylindrical tunnels by replacement of imidazole group with triazole group in the ligand. As a result, MOF 2 holds a higher density of active sites and Lewis acid metallic sites in the surface of nanotube channels, making the $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ capture and separation of MOF 2 is greater than that of $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ at $298\mathrm{~K~}$ . This work may supply an effective strategy to build new different MOFs with good performances via various functionalized organic linkers and large radius alkaline earth ions as well as reducing the environmental pollution of the alkaline earth ions.
